# Accepted CVEs — the visible risk register for image scanning.
# Every entry needs: CVE id, image, reason, review-by date.
# Gate policy: CRITICAL + --ignore-unfixed (unfixable OS-package CVEs are
# visible in the SBOM artifacts but do not fail CI — nothing actionable).

# pgvector/pgvector:pg16 — Go stdlib crypto/tls in the bundled gosu binary.
# gosu runs once at container init to drop root->postgres and makes no TLS
# connections; the vulnerable code path is unreachable. Upstream pg16 tag has
# not rebuilt (digest identical to our pin). Review: next pgvector image bump
# or 2026-12-01, whichever first.
CVE-2025-68121

# ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui (pinned main digest) — GitPython RCE via
# crafted remote repo, fixed in 3.1.59. Compensating controls: the namespace
# is egress-locked (CNP: litellm/postgres/DNS only), so the pod cannot clone
# remote repositories at all, and OFFLINE_MODE disables the online import
# paths. The current upstream :main build fixes GitPython but adds 4 new
# fixable CRITICALs (nltk RCE x3, unstructured SSRF) — bumping is a net
# regression today. Review: 2026-10-01 against upstream releases.
CVE-2026-78676
